sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To circumscribe a circle about a given square.
----
proof:

Let *ABCD* be the given square.

It is required to circumscribe a circle about the square *ABCD.*

Join *AC* and *BD,* and let them cut one another at *E.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.9 diagram" src="propIV9.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.9",
        pivot: "E",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;140,30",
            "C;point;free;140,235",
            "E;point;midpoint;A,C;black;green",
            "ABCD;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;black;random",
            "B;point;perpendicular;E,A",
            "D;point;perpendicular;E,C",
            "square;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then, since *DA* equals *AB,* and *AC* is common, therefore the two sides *DA* and *AC* equal the two sides *BA* and *AC,* and the base *DC* equals the base *BC,* therefore the angle *DAC* equals the angle *BAC.* [!just I.8]

Therefore the angle *DAB* is bisected by *AC.*

Similarly we can prove that each of the angles *ABC, BCD,* and *CDA* is bisected by the straight lines *AC* and *DB.*

Now, since the angle *DAB* equals the angle *ABC,* and the angle *EAB* is half of the angle *DAB,* and the angle *EBA* half of the angle *ABC,* therefore the angle *EAB* also equals the angle *EBA,* so that the side *EA* also equals *EB.* [!just I.6]

Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines *EA* and *EB* equals each of the straight lines *EC* and *ED.*

Therefore the four straight lines *EA, EB, EC,* and *ED* equal one another.

Therefore the circle described with center *E* and radius one of the straight lines *EA,* *EB, EC,* or *ED* also passes through the remaining points, and it is circumscribed about the square *ABCD.*

Let it be circumscribed, as *ABCD.*

Therefore a circle has been circumscribed about the given square.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
